WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.585 --> 00:00:03.879
- We're... concerned.

00:00:06.131 --> 00:00:08.550
The Soviets might be trying to
introduce a new weapon.

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:12.387
- We let this go...

00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:18.227
...it would set
a dangerous precedent.

00:00:20.771 --> 00:00:21.813
- Welcome to NASA.

00:00:22.439 --> 00:00:25.901
You are, as of this moment,
officially astronaut candidates.

00:00:27.277 --> 00:00:30.239
- Some day people will
write the history of this time.

00:00:30.781 --> 00:00:33.242
- This is Jamestown actual.
Ten seconds... mark.

00:00:34.159 --> 00:00:37.538
- They will say that during
the coldest depths of the Cold War,

00:00:37.621 --> 00:00:38.372
(alarm chirps)

00:00:39.081 --> 00:00:41.333
- America inspired the world.

00:00:41.416 --> 00:00:44.086
♪ Sweet dreams are made of this ♪

00:00:44.169 --> 00:00:45.671
- I give you Pathfinder.

00:00:46.338 --> 00:00:48.340
It's three times as powerful
as our current shuttles.

00:00:50.050 --> 00:00:52.344
- I'm tired of talking about
the good ol' days.

00:00:53.136 --> 00:00:54.429
(laughs)

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:56.265
- Don't y'all miss it?

00:00:56.348 --> 00:00:58.976
♪ Some of them want to use you ♪

00:00:59.059 --> 00:01:02.521
- With this weapon, they could
drop munitions on any point on Earth.

00:01:03.522 --> 00:01:04.606
♪ Some of them want to be... ♪

00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:07.276
- The President wants you to put
together a new mission.

00:01:09.111 --> 00:01:10.279
- I shouldn't go.

00:01:12.239 --> 00:01:14.908
- You don't think I notice the look
in your eyes at every launch?

00:01:14.992 --> 00:01:15.826
- Hoorah.

00:01:17.077 --> 00:01:20.622
♪ Sweet dreams are made of this ♪

00:01:21.373 --> 00:01:24.126
- I have here the rules of engagement
for use of force on the Moon.

00:01:24.668 --> 00:01:26.128
♪ Travel the world and... ♪

00:01:26.211 --> 00:01:28.172
- That's steps away from nuclear war.

00:01:28.714 --> 00:01:29.673
- Target lock.

00:01:29.756 --> 00:01:32.301
- Once we do this thing,
there's no going back.

00:01:33.177 --> 00:01:34.595
(alarm blaring)

00:01:38.849 --> 00:01:40.350
- This program...

00:01:40.893 --> 00:01:43.270
...has the power
to change the world.

00:01:46.857 --> 00:01:48.609
- You need to remind them of Apollo 11.

00:01:50.485 --> 00:01:53.113
- We came in peace for all mankind

00:01:53.197 --> 00:01:54.156
- Ready to fire.

00:01:55.407 --> 00:01:57.201
- We need to live up to that.

